- What is the time/space complexity and how can you optimize further for large n?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP state augmentation for a path with a constrained number of turns, combining path optimization with reconstruction. It demands careful handling of transitions when direction changes. 

## Key Concepts
- DP on grid paths with turn constraints
- 4D state dp[i][j][t][dir]
- Reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time: O(n*m*k); Space: O(n*m*k)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPathWithKTurns(grid, K) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () =>
    Array.from({length: m}, () => Array.from({length: K+1}, () => [NEG, NEG]))
  );
  dp[0][0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  dp[0][0][0][1] = grid[0][0];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      if (i === 0 && j === 0) continue;
      for (let t = 0; t <= K; t++) {
        const val = grid[i][j];
        if (j > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t][0], dp[i][j-1][t][0] + val);
          if (t > 0) dp[i][j][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t][0], dp[i][j-1][t-1][1] + val);
        }
        if (i > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t][1] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t][1], dp[i-1][j][t][1] + val);
          if (t > 0) dp[i][j][t][1] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t][1], dp[i-1][j][t-1][0] + val);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction would backtrack using stored choices (omitted for brevity)
  return {dp, best: Math.max(...Array.from({length:K+1}, (_,t)=>Math.max(dp[n-1][m-1][t][0], dp[n-1][m-1][t][1])))};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests a beginner-friendly DP pattern for selecting exactly k non-overlapping contiguous subarrays with a per-subarray cost. It forces candidates to choose between extending a current subarray and starting a new one, while also testing reconstruction and space-time trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- **DP state separation**: Maintaining 'best' (completed subarrays) vs 'active' (subarray currently being built)
- **Non-overlapping interval selection** with a fixed count constraint
- **Reconstruction** of the chosen subarrays from DP tables
- **Space optimization** using rolling arrays (2D → 1D)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  const best = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const active = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));

  best[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      best[i][t] = Math.max(best[i-1][t], active[i-1][t]);

      if (t > 0) {
        active[i][t] = Math.max(
          active[i-1][t] + A[i-1],
          best[i-1][t-1] + A[i-1] - c
        );
      }
    }
  }

  return best[n][k];
}
```

**Time Complexity**: O(n × k)
**Space Complexity**: O(n × k), or O(k) with rolling arrays.
